    topic: "Flight change announcement",
    audioText: "Good evening, ladies and gentlemen, and welcome to the departures hall at Istanbul airport. This is an important announcement for all passengers travelling on the Uzbekistan Air flight to Tashkent. We regret to inform you that the flight, which was originally scheduled to leave at nine fifteen, will now depart later than planned. At first, our ground staff believed the delay would be thirteen minutes, but I have just been told that the aircraft arrived from Baku with a technical fault in its landing equipment, so the delay will in fact be thirty minutes at the very least. Please ignore the earlier message on the screens. The new departure time is therefore nine forty five, and we will confirm this again in twenty minutes.\n\nThere is also a change of gate. You were originally told to go to gate fourteen, and many of you have already queued there. I am sorry, that gate has now been closed for cleaning. Please make your way to gate forty, which is at the far end of the main corridor, beyond the duty free shops. It takes about ten minutes on foot, so please do not leave it until the last moment. Passengers who need help with wheelchairs or small children should speak to any member of staff in a yellow jacket, and a free buggy service is running every five minutes from the information desk.\n\nBecause of the delay, the airline would like to offer every adult passenger a meal voucher. The voucher is worth fifteen euros and may be used in any restaurant on the upper floor, but not in the coffee bars downstairs, which do not accept them. Please note that the voucher cannot be exchanged for cash, and alcohol is not included. Passengers under the age of eighteen will receive a smaller voucher, worth ten euros. If you would like to collect yours, go to the desk next to gate thirty eight, where two colleagues will check your boarding pass. You do not need to show your passport.\n\nSome of you have asked whether the flight might be cancelled altogether. At the moment, we do not expect that, although I must be honest and say that the engineers have not yet finished their inspection. If the problem turns out to be more serious than they think, we will arrange hotel rooms and transport for everyone, and there will be an announcement before ten fifteen. Passengers with a connecting flight from Tashkent to Samarkand have been contacted separately, and a seat has been kept for them on the later evening service, so they should not worry. Those who checked in bags do not need to collect them; your luggage will stay on the aircraft and be loaded as soon as possible.\n\nFinally, may I thank you for your patience. We know that nobody enjoys waiting, especially after a long day, and we sincerely apologise for the inconvenience. Our staff will be happy to answer any further questions at gate forty. Thank you.",
